# Frontend Design — Skills-First Workflow

All frontend design and UI work in this project MUST use installed agent skills. Never hand-write UI from scratch without running the skill workflow below.

## Required Skills (read before coding)

| Priority | Skill | Path | When |
|----------|-------|------|------|
| 1 | ui-ux-pro-max | `.cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/SKILL.md` | Every UI/UX task — design system, colors, typography, UX rules |
| 2 | 21st-cache | `.cursor/skills/21st-cache/SKILL.md` | **Cache-first** — check `.21st/cache/` before any 21st API/MCP call |
| 3 | 21st-cli-use | `.agents/skills/21st-cli-use/SKILL.md` | Search/install components from 21st.dev before building |
| 4 | 21st-ai | `.agents/skills/21st-ai/SKILL.md` | Generate or iterate UI via 21st AI |
| 5 | frontend-design | `.agents/skills/frontend-design/SKILL.md` | Distinctive aesthetic direction, avoid generic AI slop |
| 6 | high-end-visual-design | `.agents/skills/high-end-visual-design/SKILL.md` | Premium polish, Awwwards-tier visuals |
| 7 | web-design-guidelines | `.agents/skills/web-design-guidelines/SKILL.md` | Audit accessibility, UX, and interface compliance |
| 8 | vercel-react-best-practices | `.agents/skills/vercel-react-best-practices/SKILL.md` | React performance and rendering patterns |

## Workflow (follow in order)

1. **Read** `ui-ux-pro-max` skill and run design-system search:
   ```bash
   python3 .cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py "<product> <style> <industry>" --design-system -p "Habits"
   ```
2. **Search 21st.dev** via `21st-cache` wrapper (cache-first) + `21st-cli-use`:
   ```bash
   python3 .cursor/skills/21st-cache/scripts/run.py search "<component query>" --limit 10 --json
   ```
3. **Apply** `frontend-design` + `high-end-visual-design` for aesthetic direction.
4. **Implement** using project tokens (`pwa/src/styles/tokens.css`) and existing UI components.
5. **Audit** with `web-design-guidelines` before finishing.
6. **Optimize** React code per `vercel-react-best-practices`.

## Rules

- Announce which skill you are using: "Using [skill] to [purpose]"
- Match existing conventions in `pwa/src/components/ui/` and `tokens.css`
- No generic fonts (Inter, Roboto, Arial) or purple-gradient defaults unless design system specifies them
- Prefer 21st.dev catalog components over custom implementations when a close match exists
- **Always cache 21st steps** — use `run.py` wrapper or save MCP responses to `.21st/cache/`; never repeat metered calls for the same query
